 "last_title": "PNG (Portable Network Graphics) Home Site",
 "last_page_text": "If you're using a\nWindows\nversion of\nNetscape Navigator\nand want to print this page (and still be able to read it), click on the\npng-printable\nlink at the very bottom of this page.\nPortable Network Graphics\nAn Open, Extensible Image Format with Lossless Compression\n(Not Related to Papua New Guinea, the Pawnee National Grassland, the Professional Numismatists Guild or the \"Pack 'N' Go\" format)\n(\nNot\nRelated to Papua New Guinea, the Pawnee National Grassland,\nthe Professional Numismatists Guild or the \"Pack 'N' Go\" format)\nWelcome to the PNG Home Site, maintained by\n. Our hero likes to speak of himself in the third person, but don't let that put you off; this is intended to be a mostly serious set of reference pages for locating information, applications and programming code related to the 31-year-old PNG image format.\nCanonical URL:\n(California, USA)\nNote that the PNG home site has moved four times since 1995 (though the URL has changed only three times, and hopefully never again). The current site is hosted by the excellent folks at\n.\nThe PNG web site is organized into four basic categories of information (blue and white headings below), not counting the separate\n(covering PNG's animated and lossy cousins). A\nto the 110+ pages is available, but the basics are summarized here.\nThe\nbelow is worth reading both for general background and for a summary of PNG's main features, but most non-programmers will probably find the\n, the\n, and perhaps the\nto be of the greatest interest and utility. The\n, on the other hand, are no longer particularly important (or maintained), insofar as virtually every image-related application has supported PNG natively--and well--for more than a decade. They too are now historical in nature.\n(\nrecommended for new visitors\n)\n(\nrecommended for new visitors\n)\n(\nrecommended for new visitors\n)\n(and a\n)\n(includes\nmailing lists\n)\n(\n)\n(also\n)\nPNG Programming Information:\nPNG Images:\n(also\n)\n(includes links to screenshots)",
